{"title":"1985 AIME Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Law_of_Cosines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Law of Cosines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallel\" title=\"Parallel\">parallel</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chord\" title=\"Chord\">chords</a> of lengths 2, 3, and 4 determine <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Central_angle\" title=\"Central angle\">central angles</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc5ed23e7b3ce8f560fe6e93ac88d6c9055900d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radian\" title=\"Radian\">radians</a>, respectively, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/f/0bf85358d0e9c2c6c42978dd2742247bdc68cdd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta &lt; \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de8ac3aa0141ebb385492cbbe6f978f6c73b655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\alpha$\" width=\"38\" height=\"8\" />, which is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rational_number\" title=\"Rational number\">rational number</a>, is expressed as a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fraction\" title=\"Fraction\">fraction</a> in lowest terms, what is the sum of its numerator and denominator?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc44394730c0756402714001ccba571e69a1bf7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200);  pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.8); real r = 8/15^0.5, a = 57.91, b = 93.135; pair O = (0,0), A = r*expi(pi/3); D(CR(O,r)); D(O--rotate(a/2)*A--rotate(-a/2)*A--cycle); D(O--rotate(b/2)*A--rotate(-b/2)*A--cycle); D(O--rotate((a+b)/2)*A--rotate(-(a+b)/2)*A--cycle); MP(&quot;2&quot;,(rotate(a/2)*A+rotate(-a/2)*A)/2,NE); MP(&quot;3&quot;,(rotate(b/2)*A+rotate(-b/2)*A)/2,NE); MP(&quot;4&quot;,(rotate((a+b)/2)*A+rotate(-(a+b)/2)*A)/2,NE); D(anglemark(rotate(-(a+b)/2)*A,O,rotate((a+b)/2)*A,5)); label(&quot;\\(\\alpha+\\beta\\)&quot;,(0.08,0.08),NE,fontsize(8)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"335\" /></center>\n<p>All chords of a given length in a given circle subtend the same <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arc\" title=\"Arc\">arc</a> and therefore the same central angle.  Thus, by the given, we can re-arrange our chords into a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> with the circle as its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcircle\" title=\"Circumcircle\">circumcircle</a>.  \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0618ad736b55ffe052dd977aed3aa0c72dca89d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200);  pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.8); real r = 8/15^0.5, a = 57.91, b = 93.135; pair O = (0,0), A = r*expi(pi/3), A1 = rotate(a/2)*A, A2 = rotate(-a/2)*A, A3 = rotate(-a/2-b)*A; D(CR(O,r)); D(O--A1--A2--cycle); D(O--A2--A3--cycle); D(O--A1--A3--cycle); MP(&quot;2&quot;,(A1+A2)/2,NE); MP(&quot;3&quot;,(A2+A3)/2,E); MP(&quot;4&quot;,(A1+A3)/2,E); D(anglemark(A2,O,A1,5)); D(anglemark(A3,O,A2,5)); label(&quot;\\(\\alpha\\)&quot;,(0.07,0.16),NE,fontsize(8)); label(&quot;\\(\\beta\\)&quot;,(0.12,-0.16),NE,fontsize(8)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"335\" /></center>\n<p>This triangle has <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Semiperimeter\" title=\"Semiperimeter\">semiperimeter</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8ded92f3393a18f87208acb06ecdfaf6fbf5c1cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 + 3 + 4}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" /> so by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Heron%27s_formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Heron&#39;s formula\">Heron's formula</a> it has <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/266e27959a783915f4b0f4c890072edfd3272154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = \\sqrt{\\frac92 \\cdot \\frac52 \\cdot \\frac32 \\cdot \\frac12} = \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"221\" height=\"43\" />.  The area of a given triangle with sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> and circumradius of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is also given by the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81ac8c3392877352d78ad290aa51fd521895a50b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = \\frac{abc}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d97b5cd21484d53be5a14a9d235b85b7ee11d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac6R = \\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98bb2912fb69c913cea3962a4d27bab2ed6c1b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\frac8{\\sqrt{15}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"74\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Now, consider the triangle formed by two radii and the chord of length 2.  This <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\">isosceles triangle</a> has vertex angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, so by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10fa5c3d8e64fbdaf60209d497940a5bba7fe5c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^2 = R^2 + R^2 - 2R^2\\cos \\alpha \\Longrightarrow \\cos \\alpha = \\frac{2R^2 - 4}{2R^2} = \\frac{17}{32}\\]\" width=\"413\" height=\"39\" />\nand the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc42264ceedbbf62ad816beaefcc708ee9d58c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 + 32 = \\boxed{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fHFD0TEfBnA?si=DRKVU_As7Rv0ou5D\">https://youtu.be/fHFD0TEfBnA?si=DRKVU_As7Rv0ou5D</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Law_of_Cosines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Law_of_Cosines)\">Solution 2 (Law of Cosines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Law of Cosines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448c27a4bb9a18d7576a79968b61141e098c460b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200);  pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.8); real r = 8/15^0.5, a = 57.91, b = 93.135; pair O = (0,0), A = r*expi(pi/3), A1 = rotate(a/2)*A, A2 = rotate(-a/2)*A, A3 = rotate(-a/2-b)*A; D(CR(O,r)); D(O--A1--A2--cycle); D(O--A2--A3--cycle); D(O--A1--A3--cycle); MP(&quot;2&quot;,(A1+A2)/2,NE); MP(&quot;3&quot;,(A2+A3)/2,E); MP(&quot;4&quot;,(A1+A3)/2,E); D(anglemark(A2,O,A1,5)); D(anglemark(A3,O,A2,5)); D(anglemark(A2,A3,A1,18)); label(&quot;\\(\\alpha\\)&quot;,(0.07,0.16),NE,fontsize(8)); label(&quot;\\(\\beta\\)&quot;,(0.12,-0.16),NE,fontsize(8)); label(&quot;\\(\\alpha\\)/2&quot;,(0.82,-1.25),NE,fontsize(8)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"335\" /></center>\n<p>It’s easy to see in triangle which lengths 2, 3, and 4, that the angle opposite the side 2 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbde502f490f5670cfad7d095cf2673932cc4ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"14\" height=\"33\" />, and using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, we get:  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/233aebba0662e3728f7166863908af375636495b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^2 = 3^2 + 4^2 - 2\\cdot3\\cdot4\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"32\" /> \nWhich, rearranges to: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c8347a23f80f954db15590485dc7587d3b34ecfb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[21 = 24\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"32\" /> \nAnd, that gets us: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c889118bf07fb02200f73912aa1803bbe845f4d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2} = 7/8\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"32\" /> \nUsing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/4/0e447d48fff5765d04b4a54380e635e0a07e3f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2\\theta = 2\\cos^2 \\theta - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />, we get that: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e051c3afff97a061a21b13d87307aeae32a56cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\alpha = 17/32\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />  \nWhich gives an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b8af8111c12dfcef0b504649333e872c721ec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><br />\n- AlexLikeMath\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(trig)\">Solution 3 (trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the first diagram above,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c565ffb7ca7b1311478b01815708d7faed6a38e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\frac{\\alpha}{2} = \\frac{1}{r}\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/74449c28f22e1ecc5e316303b0b0e198aea2ab61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\frac{\\beta}{2} = \\frac{1.5}{r}\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0165083dc7a62419987a607b356c16a23d3b54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}+\\frac{\\beta}{2})=\\frac{2}{r}\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"38\" />\nby the Pythagorean trig identities,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689ba5facb68d75e872385fd1ee3fe339566e219.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\frac{\\alpha}{2}=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{r^2}}\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05ed39db5b524e7e4c12f5c19ff5c5bd1f7c26c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\frac{\\beta}{2}=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{2.25}{r^2}}\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"43\" />\nso by the composite sine identity\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e5bb48870d62c1987781dcaa4f4337d102492b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{r}=\\frac{1}{r}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{2.25}{r^2}}+\\frac{1.5}{r}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{r^2}}\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"43\" />\nmultiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5745df50c8607bdc9b8de4968315633a3047dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, then subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a2533abc5f440f1f06fc1abdc49edc6ac12cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{4-\\frac{9}{r^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"69\" height=\"43\" /> from both sides\nsquaring both sides, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53cd71714109465ae9e3e95a3bd53d136407764.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16 - 8\\sqrt{4-\\frac{9}{r^2}} + 4 - \\frac{9}{r^2}=9 - \\frac{9}{r^2}\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c257ceba7b781ab705f3129a1613bbc1984932a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow 16+4=9+8\\sqrt{4-\\frac{9}{r^2}}\\Longrightarrow\\frac{11}{8}=\\sqrt{4-\\frac{9}{r^2}}\\Longrightarrow\\frac{121}{64}=4-\\frac{9}{r^2}\\]\" width=\"492\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cf48869084145c123074025be820ad9aba36d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow\\frac{(256-121)r^2}{64}=9\\Longrightarrow r^2= \\frac{64}{15}\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"39\" />\nplugging this back in,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/14911fb6e98b7f46d473d130bf7fd26fe4b9d041.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos^2(\\frac{\\alpha}{2})=1-\\frac{15}{64}=\\frac{49}{64}\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0de3232fd81e76ab6b832b20a55a9cd28a6978c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\alpha)=2(\\frac{49}{64})-1=\\frac{34}{64}=\\frac{17}{32}\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"38\" />\nand the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af6cfafd5578d97309db507b4759d1633e79b20f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17+32=\\boxed{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME\" title=\"1985 AIME\">1985 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1985 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1985 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AIME_Problems/